        {
            "number": 4,
            "revision": "911df9ee351212a537f93065cc34446b76d4d55c",
            "parents": [
                "c5fb130e6e891676a19f6af750f66f688fbd30e1"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/03/79803/4",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Patrick NC Lin",
                "email": "patrick.nc.lin.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                "username": "PatrickLinww"
            },
            "createdOn": 1745235099,
            "author": {
                "name": "Patrick NC Lin",
                "email": "patrick.nc.lin.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                "username": "PatrickLinww"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "There is no such thing as a \"presence sensor\"."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick NC Lin",
                        "email": "patrick.nc.lin.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "PatrickLinww"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi Patrick,\nThe reason for adding this virtual sensor is to meet the thermal requirements. The thermal team has indicated that when the CXL connector is not connected, the associated sensors should be in a \"missing\" state (i.e., sensor fail), and the fan duty should be increased to 100%. \nHowever, due to hardware limitations, when MCIO3 is not connected, the WF cannot initialize, and when MCIO4 is not connected, the I3C cannot establish a connection with the WF BIC. These hardware constraints result in the BMC not including the associated sensors in the sensor list. In other words, the BMC will not monitor these sensors and will not trigger the fail-safe mode due to these sensor failures.\n\nTo address this issue, we propose adding this virtual sensor to monitor the CXL connector status. This virtual sensor will also be included in the fan control table. If any CXL connector on any slot is not properly inserted, the fan speed will be increased accordingly to meet the thermal requirements. (https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/79806)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "@patrick.nc.lin.wiwynn@gmail.com I am with Patrick on this one. There is nothing like a presence sensor and you will only find yourself fighting an uphill battle here."
                }
            ],
